<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <RootNamespace>RestApi._00.CommonFunctionality</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>RestApi.00.CommonFunctionality</AssemblyName>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- *Migration Note: the foundational library for the entire OnBase Document Management
       (REST) API training set, models and configuration types only, no connection logic
       (that's RestApi.01.ConnectingToOnBase). Deliberately self-contained, the same way
       Unity.00.CommonFunctionality avoids depending on CSharp.SharedLibrary: no reference
       to any Unity.*.* project here, even though several types below are close
       counterparts to ones there (DatabankException, DataProtectionExtensions,
       AuthenticationMode), each is its own independent copy, adapted for this track. See
       LectureNotes.md.

       net10.0, not net48: unlike the Unity.*.* track, nothing here depends on
       Hyland.Unity (a .NET-Framework-only assembly), the REST API is plain HTTP, so
       there's no architectural reason to stay on net48. System.Configuration.ConfigurationManager
       is still used for the same App.config-style ConfigurationSection/ConfigurationElement
       pattern Unity.00 uses (via its own NuGet package, which supports modern .NET), so
       Settings' "Save to config" behavior can work the same way across both the Unity and
       REST API versions of the harness.

       Secret encryption uses Microsoft.AspNetCore.DataProtection's IDataProtector, not
       Unity.00's DPAPI-via-registry (aspnet_setreg.exe) approach, a deliberate choice
       once this track was no longer tied to net48. Despite the ASP.NET Core-sounding
       package name, it works fine in any .NET app; the standalone, non-DI-container entry
       point (DataProtectionProvider.Create(DirectoryInfo), used here since there's no
       service collection to hang IDataProtectionProvider off of) specifically lives in
       Microsoft.AspNetCore.DataProtection.Extensions, a separate package from the base
       one, which only provides the interfaces and the DI-based AddDataProtection() setup.
       See DataProtectionExtensions and LectureNotes.md. -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="System.Configuration.ConfigurationManager" Version="10.0.12" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.DataProtection.Extensions" Version="10.0.12" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" />
    <None Include="LectureNotes.md" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
